<xml>
  <block type="st_sd" x="20" y="20">
    <mutation uid="card40" />
    <field name="NAME">card</field>
    <field name="CS">10</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="480" h="240">Purpose: Convert a polar servo/distance scan into row-ordered BMP output on SD. Advanced example with tight AVR memory margins.
Wiring: SPI SD card: CS D10; Servo: PIN D9; HC-SR04: TRIG D5, ECHO D6; SPI MOSI D11, MISO D12, SCK D13; CS as listed. Common GND; use each module’s required supply.
Try: Change the pixel/intensity mapping after understanding the polar-to-raster conversion.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="device_servo" x="300" y="20">
    <mutation uid="pan40" />
    <field name="NAME">pan</field>
    <field name="PIN">9</field>
    <field name="ENGINE">CORE</field>
  </block>
  <block type="device_ultrasonic" x="540" y="20">
    <mutation uid="range40" />
    <field name="NAME">range</field>
    <field name="TRIG">5</field>
    <field name="ECHO">6</field>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_setup_section" x="20" y="170">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="controls_if">
        <value name="IF0">
          <block type="st_sd_ok">
            <field name="DEVICE">card40</field>
            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">True when the most recent operation on this card succeeded. Check it before using data from a read or continuing a file write.</comment>
          </block>
        </value>
        <statement name="DO0">
          <block type="st_bmp_stream_create">
            <field name="DEVICE">card40</field>
            <field name="RESERVE">false</field>
            <value name="PATH">
              <block type="text">
                <field name="TEXT">POLAR.BMP</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <value name="WIDTH">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">128</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <value name="HEIGHT">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">61</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <next>
              <block type="controls_if">
                <value name="IF0">
                  <block type="st_sd_ok">
                    <field name="DEVICE">card40</field>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">True when the most recent operation on this card succeeded. Check it before using data from a read or continuing a file write.</comment>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <statement name="DO0">
                  <block type="controls_for">
                    <field name="VAR">angle</field>
                    <value name="FROM">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">0</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="TO">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">180</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="BY">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">3</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <statement name="DO">
                      <block type="device_servo_write">
                        <field name="DEVICE">pan40</field>
                        <value name="ANGLE">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">angle</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <next>
                          <block type="base_delay">
                            <value name="DELAY_TIME">
                              <block type="math_number">
                                <field name="NUM">80</field>
                              </block>
                            </value>
                            <next>
                              <block type="arduino_typed_variable">
                                <field name="TYPE">int</field>
                                <field name="VAR">distance</field>
                                <value name="VALUE">
                                  <block type="device_ultrasonic_read">
                                    <field name="DEVICE">range40</field>
                                  </block>
                                </value>
                                <next>
                                  <block type="controls_for">
                                    <field name="VAR">radius</field>
                                    <value name="FROM">
                                      <block type="math_number">
                                        <field name="NUM">0</field>
                                      </block>
                                    </value>
                                    <value name="TO">
                                      <block type="math_number">
                                        <field name="NUM">127</field>
                                      </block>
                                    </value>
                                    <value name="BY">
                                      <block type="math_number">
                                        <field name="NUM">1</field>
                                      </block>
                                    </value>
                                    <statement name="DO">
                                      <block type="st_bmp_append_pixel">
                                        <field name="DEVICE">card40</field>
                                        <value name="WHITE">
                                          <block type="logic_operation">
                                            <field name="OP">AND</field>
                                            <value name="A">
                                              <block type="logic_compare">
                                                <field name="OP">GT</field>
                                                <value name="A">
                                                  <block type="variables_get">
                                                    <field name="VAR">distance</field>
                                                  </block>
                                                </value>
                                                <value name="B">
                                                  <block type="math_number">
                                                    <field name="NUM">0</field>
                                                  </block>
                                                </value>
                                              </block>
                                            </value>
                                            <value name="B">
                                              <block type="logic_compare">
                                                <field name="OP">EQ</field>
                                                <value name="A">
                                                  <block type="variables_get">
                                                    <field name="VAR">radius</field>
                                                  </block>
                                                </value>
                                                <value name="B">
                                                  <block type="variables_get">
                                                    <field name="VAR">distance</field>
                                                  </block>
                                                </value>
                                              </block>
                                            </value>
                                          </block>
                                        </value>
                                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Append the next pixel in scan order. The image writer packs the file format as it streams, so the complete image need not fit in RAM.</comment>
                                      </block>
                                    </statement>
                                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Repeat the body with radius taking each value from the start to the end, using the given step. Array indices start at zero.</comment>
                                  </block>
                                </next>
                                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create distance as int. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
                              </block>
                            </next>
                            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Wait for the given number of milliseconds (1000 ms = 1 second). This pauses the main program; avoid long waits when loop must service motors, music files or serial input.</comment>
                          </block>
                        </next>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Send a target position to the named servo. The library keeps generating pulses; reaching the target takes mechanical time. Position mode uses degrees, pulse mode uses microseconds.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </statement>
                    <next>
                      <block type="st_bmp_stream_finish">
                        <field name="DEVICE">card40</field>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Finish and close the image file after all expected pixels. An incomplete scan is reported as an error rather than a complete image.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </next>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Repeat the body with angle taking each value from the start to the end, using the given step. Array indices start at zero.</comment>
                  </block>
                </statement>
              </block>
            </next>
          </block>
        </statement>
      </block>
    </statement>
  </block>
</xml>
